# NIROS Project Philosophy

## Mission

NIROS is a practical software system that helps understand a person well enough to support thoughtful, safe, personalized care pathways. It is not an academic research project. Build software that runs, can be tested, and can be reviewed by humans.

## Current priority

The **Human Understanding Engine** is the active focus. Other modules (Therapeutic Engine, Music Engine, sensors, voice, UI) wait until the HUE MVP is working or the user explicitly expands scope.

## How we work

- **MVP first.** Ship the smallest end-to-end slice that proves the idea, then iterate.
- **Working code over perfect architecture.** Prefer a runnable implementation today over a grand design for tomorrow.
- **Obsidian is the source of truth.** The vault defines what NIROS is and what we are building. Read it; do not reinvent it.
- **Cursor is the implementation environment.** Code lives in the repo; the vault guides it. Do not move product truth into code comments or ad-hoc docs.
- **Preserve the vault architecture.** Do not rename stable top-level modules or reorganize the vault without explicit approval.
- **No unnecessary documentation.** Do not create docs, essays, or vault pages unless they directly unblock implementation.
- **No unnecessary research.** Do not expand literature reviews, speculative design, or parallel explorations unless the user asks.

## Quality principles

- **Modular, testable code.** Small modules, clear boundaries, automated tests for behavior that matters.
- **Explainable psychology.** Hypotheses, profiles, and recommendations must trace to evidence — not opaque labels or black-box judgments.
- **Safety first.** Risk screening, consent, and human review are constraints on every flow — not features added later.

## Agent team

Use the NIROS subagents in `.cursor/agents/` for specialized work. This rule sets philosophy; agents and vault docs carry implementation detail.

## Test execution

The AI must never automatically execute project tests.

The AI may:
- create tests;
- modify tests;
- update fixtures.

The AI must never run:
- pytest
- python -m pytest
- uv run pytest
- poetry run pytest
- any terminal-based test command.

The developer executes all tests manually.